      "readingAid": "eo",
      "pronunciation": "Close to the vowel in “sun,” short and pure. You’ll hear it in 어.",
      "audioText": "어",
      "forms": []
    },
    {
      "symbol": "ㅗ",
      "readingAid": "o",
      "pronunciation": "Like the vowel in “go,” but short and pure, with no “w” glide. You’ll hear it in 오.",
      "audioText": "오",
      "forms": []
    },
    {
      "symbol": "ㅜ",
      "readingAid": "u",
      "pronunciation": "Like the vowel in “food,” but short and pure. You’ll hear it in 우.",
      "audioText": "우",
      "forms": []
    },
    {
      "symbol": "ㅡ",
      "readingAid": "eu",
      "pronunciation": "There’s no exact English match: say “oo” without rounding your lips. You’ll hear it in 으.",
      "audioText": "으",
      "forms": []
    },
    {
      "symbol": "ㅣ",
      "readingAid": "i",
      "pronunciation": "Like the vowel in “see,” but short and pure. You’ll hear it in 이.",
      "audioText": "이",
      "forms": []
    },
    {
      "symbol": "ㄱ",
      "readingAid": "g",
      "pronunciation": "You’ll hear it at the start of ga. It’s a soft, unaspirated stop, with less puff of air than English k, and it isn’t a fully voiced English g.",
      "audioText": "가",
      "forms": []
